a crowning moment for europe's largest  infrastructure project  queen elizabeth lending her name to  london's biggest single transport  upgrade for more than a century  a decade in the making the line is a  journey into the future forget the  cramped tunnels of the city's 19th  century tube network this is something  else  light filled chambers serenely curved  concrete and glass it feels like a huge  modern art gallery not a mode of  transport it provides state-of-the-art  fast clean ambient services that  londoners will flock to so that plus the  economic benefit something like 42  billion pound injection to the uk  economy this truly is a game changer for  london  the trains are smoother and faster than  anything seen in the city before  speeding travellers from one side of  central london to the other in nine  minutes as the uk races to reach its  target of net zero carbon emissions by  2050 public transport is key  these are cathedral-like otherworldly  spaces designed to accommodate this  growing metropolis making the morning  commute less of a squeeze  and more of a breeze  but at 23 billion dollars it hasn't come  cheap that's 5 billion more than  expected twice the price of the london  2012 olympics or 15 buckingham palaces  the drop in passenger numbers during the  pandemics left a 1.8 billion dollar hole  in transport for london's finances and  with 20 percent fewer people using the  underground network choosing to work  from home instead  there are concerns about when this new  line will start paying for itself  the process of boring tunnels and  pouring concrete was finished years ago  returning this into the most advanced  digital railway in the world was a 120  kilometer long it nightmare this is a  probably the world's most complex fully  digital railway it undoubtedly has the  world's most complicated signaling  system with four different signaling  systems we've got 16 million digital  parts on this railway so to bring them  all together has been quite a challenge  actually but we've we kind of got there  in the end and i think customers will  reap the benefits of that  this entire project is one massive  exercise in engineering problem solving  instead of an escalator here a funicular  railway  on may the 24th when the line opens to  the public these 250 meter long  platforms will reverberate with the  sound of thousands of travelers  queen elizabeth was born in an age of  steam trains now the elizabeth line is  driving the future of digital transport  neve barca al jazeera london
 

